{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Pharaoh will lift up your head.</b> ירים [he will lift]; the correct view is that it is in the manner of counting [i.e., taking a census], and the proof is \"and he lifted up the head of the chief cupbearer and the head of the chief baker among his servants\" (Genesis 40:20). In the portion Ki Tissa I will explain this." "<b>your station.</b> Your former watch, and your position and your appointed place. It is also possible that it is from the root כן, like \"and he shall stand upon his כנו [station]\" (Daniel 11:20)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "The verse citation appears to read בראשית מ כ (Genesis 40:20) but should be Genesis 40:20, which matches the quoted verse; resolved as Genesis 40:20."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:35.161299381Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}